WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.255
A secure Blazor baseline starts with
render-mode awareness.

2
00:00:06.335 --> 00:00:11.426
Teams should understand which code runs on
the server,

3
00:00:11.506 --> 00:00:17.372
which code runs in the browser, what data
is sent to components,

4
00:00:17.452 --> 00:00:21.658
and where protected decisions are
enforced.

5
00:00:21.738 --> 00:00:26.386
Browser-executed code can guide the
experience,

6
00:00:26.466 --> 00:00:30.340
but it is not a trusted enforcement point.

7
00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:38.388
Authenticate users explicitly and
authorize protected data and state changes on the

8
00:00:38.468 --> 00:00:39.797
server or API.

9
00:00:39.877 --> 00:00:43.861
Components and routes can express intent,

10
00:00:43.941 --> 00:00:50.913
but the final decision belongs where data
is served or where operations are

11
00:00:50.993 --> 00:00:52.100
performed.

12
00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:59.595
APIs called by Blazor clients must enforce
their own identity and access rules.

13
00:00:59.675 --> 00:01:03.328
Validate input where changes are made.

14
00:01:03.408 --> 00:01:07.945
Client-side validation can improve
usability,

15
00:01:08.025 --> 00:01:14.334
but trusted backends must enforce business
rules, resource scope,

16
00:01:14.414 --> 00:01:20.280
request intent, file limits, and
state-change requirements.

17
00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:25.672
Treat browser storage, component state,
query strings,

18
00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:31.618
and hidden fields as convenience state
rather than authority.

19
00:01:31.698 --> 00:01:36.568
Handle JavaScript interop and rendering
with care.

20
00:01:36.648 --> 00:01:44.395
Preserve normal framework encoding where
possible, review any markup rendering,

21
00:01:44.475 --> 00:01:52.444
and understand the browser-side
dependencies that participate in the application.

22
00:01:52.524 --> 00:02:00.050
Do not let third-party code or convenience
interop hide important data handling

23
00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.236
decisions.

24
00:02:01.316 --> 00:02:06.297
Finally, keep secrets, logs, errors,
dependencies,

25
00:02:06.377 --> 00:02:10.472
and deployment settings production-safe.

26
00:02:10.552 --> 00:02:18.410
Secure Blazor applications are built by
connecting component design to API design,

27
00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:25.684
identity, authorization, validation,
browser state, rendering, logging,

28
00:02:25.764 --> 00:02:28.420
and operational readiness.
